sddm-authelia-passkey (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Broker: resolve the target account's UID via NSS fresh on every
    flow start (not just once at broker startup) and embed it in the
    approval marker (v2 format: VERSION=2/USERNAME=/UID=/NONCE=/
    APPROVED_AT=).
  * PAM module: re-resolve the requesting account's UID via NSS at
    marker consumption time and require an exact match against the
    marker's embedded UID - an account deleted and recreated (same
    username, different UID) between approval and login is rejected.
  * KWallet: per-user credentials (kwallet_credential_name is now a
    prefix, one systemd-creds encrypted file per allowed user - see
    scripts/setup-kwallet-credential.sh and docs/kwallet.md). The
    hand-off marker also carries UID, and kwallet-secretd refuses to
    release a secret unless the requesting UID matches it. Removed the
    v0.3.0 restriction that refused kwallet_auto_unlock with more than
    one allowed_users entry.
  * New tests/integration/pam-multiuser-test.sh proving the core
    cross-user invariant against real local test accounts and the
    compiled PAM module: alice's approval never authenticates bob and
    vice versa, parallel alice+bob approvals remain independent.
  * SDDM theme: the smartphone/passkey flow is now bound to whichever
    account SDDM's own existing user selector currently has selected
    (avatar list or manual username entry), captured immutably per
    flow; changing the selection mid-flow cancels it rather than
    silently retargeting.
  * Documented the multi-user identity-binding model in
    docs/architecture.md.

 -- Benjamin Lütker <benjamin.luetker@gmail.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0200

sddm-authelia-passkey (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Broker: refuse `allowed_users` containing root at config-load time.
  * PAM module: verify approval-marker ownership/mode (root:root, 0600)
    before trusting it, as defense in depth alongside markerDir's own
    permissions.
  * Fix debian/rules, postinst, prerm missing the executable bit in git.
  * Fix placeholder github.com/example Homepage/Source URLs in Debian
    packaging metadata.
  * Document the packaged-.deb install and rollback paths (previously
    only the build-from-source path was documented).
  * Fix tests/integration/pam-flow-test.sh referencing the wrong
    kwallet-secretd systemd unit name.
  * Replace public-facing "Pixel" wording with vendor-neutral
    "smartphone/passkey" throughout docs, config, and source comments.
  * CI: add package-build/lintian/lifecycle testing, CodeQL, govulncheck,
    gitleaks, dependency review, and theme-patch validation.
  * Expand broker test coverage for token-poll outcome classification,
    username resolution, and flow cancellation.
  * Broker: refuse kwallet_auto_unlock=true with more than one
    allowed_users entry (no per-user KWallet credential yet); document
    multi-user readiness and identity binding in docs/architecture.md.

